# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
Sandbox Test-Case Mapper
========================
Compares two source sandboxes (C files, H files and user-defined files), reports
every changed file and every changed line, analyses the whole sandbox (functions,
call graph, macro / header users) and recommends the test cases that must be
re-run for every change - each with the reasons why.

Stages:
  1. the matcher picks candidates out of 3000+ test cases in milliseconds
     (keywords, identifiers, glossary, semantic vectors learned from your test
     cases, everything learned from your training)
  2. the SMART RANKER re-orders the best 200 candidates of every change.  It is
     trained on this PC from your verdicts - nothing is downloaded:
       logistic regression | gradient-boosted trees | neural network | ensemble
     Cross-validation over your training sessions picks the best one; it is
     re-trained in the background as you keep training (needs numpy).
  3. optional LOCAL LLM: a language model on this PC reads the change and every
     candidate test case, confirms or rejects it and writes the reason.
Your own decisions (training, Confirm / Reject) always win.  All confirmed test
cases are exported to an Excel file at a path you choose.

The model is trained by a human, day by day, in the TRAINING window: marks out
of 10, Right / Wrong per test case, and the expected test cases the model missed.
Everything it learns is stored locally (default  D:\\model\\data).

100 % OFFLINE BY DESIGN
    * standard library + openpyxl (+ numpy for the smart ranker, + llama-cpp-python
      for the optional LLM)
    * no internet, no cloud service, no telemetry, no download
    * no network socket at all - not even to 127.0.0.1.  Only if you choose an
      Ollama / LM Studio server in the LOCAL LLM window may it talk to 127.0.0.1.

INPUTS
    New sandbox / Old sandbox  folders to compare
    Files-changed Excel        alternative to the old sandbox (press "Template"
                               in the GUI to get the format; only "File" is mandatory)
    Test-case Excel            one sheet, column "Text", one test case per row
    Confirmed TCs Excel        where the confirmed test cases are saved

LOCAL LLM (optional, LOCAL LLM window)
    llama.cpp  - pip install llama-cpp-python + one GGUF model file (recommended)
    Ollama / LM Studio / llama-server running on this PC

RUN
    python sandbox_tc_mapper.py                 -> GUI
    python sandbox_tc_mapper.py --selftest      -> built-in self-test suite
    python sandbox_tc_mapper.py --benchmark     -> simulated training on demo data
    python sandbox_tc_mapper.py --compare-models [--testcases TC.xlsx] [--ranker auto|off|lr|gbdt|mlp|ensemble]
                                                -> compare the ranking models on your training data
                                                   (with --testcases: rebuild from the training log first)
    python sandbox_tc_mapper.py --model-benchmark -> all ranking models on unseen synthetic changes
    python sandbox_tc_mapper.py --make-demo DIR -> demo sandboxes + 3000+ test cases
    python sandbox_tc_mapper.py --llm-test --gguf MODEL.gguf      -> test a local LLM
    python sandbox_tc_mapper.py --llm-benchmark --gguf MODEL.gguf -> matcher vs LLM on demo data
    python sandbox_tc_mapper.py --old A --new B --testcases TC.xlsx --out R.xlsx
           [--gguf MODEL.gguf | --llm] [--confirmed-out CONFIRMED.xlsx]  -> headless run

Requires: Python 3.9+,  openpyxl  (tkinter ships with Python on Windows);
          numpy is optional (smart ranker, semantic vectors).
"""
